# ── Feats (2024-07 audit, full tooltip detail) ───────────────────────────────
FEATURE_DESCS.update({
    'Actor': "Skilled at mimicry and dramatics. You have advantage on Charisma (Deception) and Charisma (Performance) checks when trying to pass yourself off as a different person. You can also mimic the speech of another person or the sounds made by other creatures, provided you've heard that person speak or that creature make the sound for at least 1 minute. A listener can tell the effect is faked with a successful Wisdom (Insight) check contested by your Charisma (Deception) check.",
    'Alert': "Always on the lookout for danger. You gain a +5 bonus to initiative. You can't be surprised while you are conscious. Other creatures don't gain advantage on attack rolls against you as a result of being unseen by you.",
    'Athlete': "You have undergone extensive physical training. When you are prone, standing up uses only 5 feet of your movement, instead of half. Climbing doesn't cost you extra movement. You can make a running long jump or a running high jump after moving only 5 feet on foot, rather than the normal 10.",
    'Charger': "When you use your action to Dash, you can use a bonus action to make one melee weapon attack or to shove a creature. If you moved at least 10 feet in a straight line immediately before taking this bonus action, you either gain a +5 bonus to the attack's damage roll (if you chose to make a melee attack and hit) or push the target up to 10 feet away from you (if you chose to shove and succeed).",
    'Crossbow Expert': "Thanks to extensive practice with the crossbow, you ignore the loading quality of crossbows with which you are proficient. Being within 5 feet of a hostile creature doesn't impose disadvantage on your ranged attack rolls. When you use the Attack action and attack with a one-handed weapon, you can use a bonus action to attack with a hand crossbow you are holding.",
    'Defensive Duelist': "Prerequisite: Dexterity 13 or higher. When you are wielding a finesse weapon with which you are proficient and another creature hits you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction to add your proficiency bonus to your AC for that attack, potentially causing the attack to miss you.",
    'Dual Wielder': "You master fighting with two weapons. You gain a +1 bonus to AC while you are wielding a separate melee weapon in each hand. You can use two-weapon fighting even when the one-handed melee weapons you are wielding aren't light. You can draw or stow two one-handed weapons when you would normally be able to draw or stow only one.",
    'Dungeon Delver': "Alert to the hidden traps and secret doors found in many dungeons. You have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Intelligence (Investigation) checks made to detect the presence of secret doors. You have advantage on saving throws made to avoid or resist traps, and resistance to the damage dealt by traps. Traveling at a fast pace doesn't impose the normal -5 penalty on your passive Wisdom (Perception) score.",
    'Durable': "Hardy and resilient. Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20. When you roll a Hit Die to regain hit points, the minimum number of hit points you regain from the roll equals twice your Constitution modifier (minimum of 2).",
    'Elemental Adept': "Prerequisite: the ability to cast at least one spell. Choose a damage type: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder. Spells you cast ignore resistance to damage of the chosen type. In addition, when you roll damage for a spell you cast that deals damage of that type, you can treat any 1 rolled on a damage die as a 2. You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different damage type each time.",
    'Grappler': "Prerequisite: Strength 13 or higher. You've developed the skills necessary to hold your own in close-quarters grappling. You have advantage on attack rolls against a creature you are grappling. You can use your action to try to pin a creature grappled by you: make another grapple check, and on a success you and the creature are both restrained until the grapple ends.",
    'Great Weapon Master': "You've learned to put the weight of a weapon to your advantage. On your turn, when you score a critical hit with a melee weapon or reduce a creature to 0 hit points with one, you can make one melee weapon attack as a bonus action. Before you make a melee attack with a heavy weapon you are proficient with, you can choose to take a -5 penalty to the attack roll; if the attack hits, you add +10 to the attack's damage.",
    'Healer': "You are an able physician. When you use a healer's kit to stabilize a dying creature, that creature also regains 1 hit point. As an action, you can spend one use of a healer's kit to tend to a creature and restore 1d6+4 hit points to it, plus additional hit points equal to the creature's maximum number of Hit Dice. The creature can't regain hit points from this feat again until it finishes a short or long rest.",
    'Heavily Armored': "Prerequisite: proficiency with medium armor. You have trained to master the use of heavy armor. Increase your Strength score by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency with heavy armor.",
    'Heavy Armor Master': "Prerequisite: proficiency with heavy armor. You can use your armor to deflect strikes that would kill others. Increase your Strength score by 1, to a maximum of 20. While you are wearing heavy armor, bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage that you take from nonmagical attacks is reduced by 3.",
    'Inspiring Leader': "Prerequisite: Charisma 13 or higher. You can spend 10 minutes inspiring your companions, shoring up their resolve to fight. Choose up to six friendly creatures (which can include yourself) within 30 feet of you who can see or hear you and who can understand you. Each creature can gain temporary hit points equal to your level + your Charisma modifier. A creature can't gain temporary hit points from this feat again until it has finished a short or long rest.",
    'Keen Mind': "You have a mind that can track time, direction, and detail with uncanny precision. Increase your Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20. You always know which way is north. You always know the number of hours left before the next sunrise or sunset. You can accurately recall anything you have seen or heard within the past month.",
    'Lightly Armored': "You have trained to master the use of light armor. Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency with light armor.",
    'Linguist': "You have studied languages and codes. Increase your Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20. You learn three languages of your choice. You can ably create written ciphers; others can't decipher a code you create unless you teach them, they succeed on an Intelligence check (DC equal to your Intelligence score + your proficiency bonus), or they use magic to decipher it.",
    'Lucky': "You have inexplicable luck that seems to kick in at just the right moment. You have 3 luck points. Whenever you make an attack roll, an ability check, or a saving throw, you can spend one luck point to roll an additional d20. You can choose to spend a luck point after you roll the die, but before the outcome is determined, and choose which of the d20s is used for the roll. You can also spend one luck point when an attack roll is made against you: roll a d20, then choose whether the attack uses the attacker's roll or yours. If more than one creature spends a luck point to influence the same roll, the points cancel each other out and no additional dice are rolled. You regain all expended luck points when you finish a long rest.",
    'Mage Slayer': "You have practiced techniques useful in melee combat against spellcasters. When a creature within 5 feet of you casts a spell, you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature. When you damage a creature that is concentrating on a spell, that creature has disadvantage on the saving throw it makes to maintain concentration. You have advantage on saving throws against spells cast by creatures within 5 feet of you.",
    'Magic Initiate': "Choose a class: bard, cleric, druid, sorcerer, warlock, or wizard. You learn two cantrips of your choice from that class's spell list. In addition, choose one 1st-level spell to learn from that same list; you can cast it once at its lowest level, and must finish a long rest before casting it this way again (you can also cast it normally with a spell slot). Your spellcasting ability for these spells depends on the class chosen: Charisma for bard, sorcerer, or warlock; Wisdom for cleric or druid; or Intelligence for wizard.",
    'Martial Adept': "You have martial training that allows you to perform special combat maneuvers. You learn two maneuvers of your choice from among those available to the Battle Master archetype (fighter class); if a maneuver requires a saving throw, the DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). You gain one superiority die, a d6 (stacking with any superiority dice from elsewhere), expended when you use a maneuver and regained on a short or long rest.",
    'Medium Armor Master': "Prerequisite: proficiency with medium armor. You have practiced moving in medium armor. Wearing medium armor doesn't impose disadvantage on your Dexterity (Stealth) checks. When you wear medium armor, you can add 3 (rather than 2) to your AC if you have a Dexterity of 16 or higher.",
    'Mobile': "You are exceptionally speedy and agile. Your speed increases by 10 feet. When you use the Dash action, difficult terrain doesn't cost you extra movement on that turn. When you make a melee attack against a creature, you don't provoke opportunity attacks from that creature for the rest of the turn, whether you hit or not.",
    'Moderately Armored': "Prerequisite: proficiency with light armor. You have trained to master the use of medium armor and shields. Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency with medium armor and shields.",
    'Mounted Combatant': "You are a dangerous foe to face while mounted. While mounted and not incapacitated, you have advantage on melee attack rolls against any unmounted creature smaller than your mount. You can force an attack targeted at your mount to target you instead. If your mount is subjected to an effect that allows it a Dexterity save to take only half damage, it instead takes no damage on a success and only half on a failure.",
    'Observant': "Quick to notice details of your environment. Increase your Intelligence or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 20. If you can see a creature's mouth while it speaks a language you understand, you can read its lips. You have a +5 bonus to your passive Wisdom (Perception) and passive Intelligence (Investigation) scores.",
    'Polearm Master': "You can keep your enemies at bay with reach weapons. When you take the Attack action and attack with only a glaive, halberd, quarterstaff, or spear, you can use a bonus action to make a melee attack with the opposite end of the weapon (same ability modifier as the primary attack; the weapon's damage die for this attack is a d4, dealing bludgeoning damage). While you are wielding a glaive, halberd, pike, quarterstaff, or spear, other creatures provoke an opportunity attack from you when they enter the reach you have with that weapon.",
    'Resilient': "Choose one ability score. Increase the chosen ability score by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency in saving throws using the chosen ability.",
    'Ritual Caster': "Prerequisite: Intelligence or Wisdom 13 or higher. You have learned a number of spells that you can cast as rituals; these spells are written in a ritual book, which you must have in hand while casting one of them. You acquire a ritual book holding two 1st-level spells of your choice from a class you pick (bard, cleric, druid, sorcerer, warlock, or wizard); the spells must have the ritual tag. That class also determines your spellcasting ability. If you come across a spell in written form (level no higher than half your level, rounded up, and with the ritual tag) on your chosen class's list, you can add it to your ritual book by spending 2 hours and 50 gp per level of the spell.",
    'Savage Attacker': "Once per turn when you roll damage for a melee weapon attack, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice and use either total.",
    'Sentinel': "You have mastered techniques to take advantage of every drop in an enemy's guard. When you hit a creature with an opportunity attack, its speed becomes 0 for the rest of the turn. Creatures provoke opportunity attacks from you even if they take the Disengage action before leaving your reach. When a creature within 5 feet of you makes an attack against a target other than you (and that target doesn't have this feat), you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against the attacking creature.",
    'Sharpshooter': "You have mastered ranged weapons and can make shots that others find impossible. Attacking at long range doesn't impose disadvantage on your ranged weapon attack rolls. Your ranged weapon attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover. Before you make an attack with a ranged weapon you are proficient with, you can choose to take a -5 penalty to the attack roll; if the attack hits, you add +10 to the attack's damage.",
    'Shield Master': "You use shields not just for protection but also for offense. While wielding a shield: if you take the Attack action on your turn, you can use a bonus action to try to shove a creature within 5 feet of you with your shield. If you aren't incapacitated, you can add your shield's AC bonus to a Dexterity save you make against a spell or other effect that targets only you. If you are subjected to an effect that allows a Dexterity save to take only half damage, you can use your reaction to take no damage on a success, interposing your shield.",
    'Skilled': "You gain proficiency in any combination of three skills or tools of your choice.",
    'Skulker': "Prerequisite: Dexterity 13 or higher. You are expert at slinking through shadows. You can try to hide when you are only lightly obscured from the creature you're hiding from. When hidden from a creature and you miss it with a ranged weapon attack, making the attack doesn't reveal your position. Dim light doesn't impose disadvantage on your Wisdom (Perception) checks relying on sight.",
    'Spell Sniper': "Prerequisite: the ability to cast at least one spell. When you cast a spell that requires an attack roll, its range is doubled. Your ranged spell attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover. You learn one cantrip that requires an attack roll, chosen from the bard, cleric, druid, sorcerer, warlock, or wizard list (spellcasting ability matches whichever list you chose from).",
    'Tavern Brawler': "Accustomed to rough-and-tumble fighting using whatever is at hand. Increase your Strength or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20. You are proficient with improvised weapons. Your unarmed strike uses a d4 for damage. When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike or improvised weapon on your turn, you can use a bonus action to attempt to grapple the target.",
    'Tough': "Your hit point maximum increases by an amount equal to twice your level when you gain this feat. Whenever you gain a level thereafter, your hit point maximum increases by an additional 2 hit points.",
    'War Caster': "Prerequisite: the ability to cast at least one spell. You have practiced casting spells in the midst of combat. You have advantage on Constitution saving throws to maintain concentration when you take damage. You can perform the somatic components of spells even with weapons or a shield in one or both hands. When a hostile creature's movement provokes an opportunity attack from you, you can use your reaction to cast a spell at it instead of making the attack (the spell must have a casting time of 1 action and target only that creature).",
    'Weapon Master': "You have practiced extensively with a variety of weapons. Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency with four weapons of your choice, each a simple or martial weapon.",

    'Crusher': "You are practiced in the art of crushing your enemies. Increase your Strength or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20. Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack that deals bludgeoning damage, you can move it 5 feet to an unoccupied space, provided the target is no more than one size larger than you. When you score a critical hit that deals bludgeoning damage, attack rolls against that creature are made with advantage until the start of your next turn.",
    'Fey Touched': "Your exposure to the Feywild's magic has changed you. Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. You learn the misty step spell and one 1st-level spell of your choice from the divination or enchantment school. You can cast each of these spells without expending a spell slot; once you cast either this way, you can't do so again with that spell until you finish a long rest (you can still cast them with spell slots you have). Spellcasting ability is the one increased by this feat.",
    'Fighting Initiate': "Prerequisite: proficiency with a martial weapon. Your martial training has helped you develop a particular style of fighting. You learn one Fighting Style option of your choice from the fighter class (if you already have one, the one you choose must differ). Whenever you reach a level that grants an Ability Score Improvement, you can replace this feat's fighting style with a different one from the fighter class.",
    'Gunner': "You have a quick hand and keen eye when employing firearms. Increase your Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency with firearms. You ignore the loading property of firearms. Being within 5 feet of a hostile creature doesn't impose disadvantage on your ranged attack rolls.",
    'Metamagic Adept': "Prerequisite: Spellcasting or Pact Magic feature. You've learned how to exert your will on your spells to alter how they function. You learn two Metamagic options of your choice from the sorcerer class; you can use only one on a spell when casting it, unless an option says otherwise (replaceable with different options whenever you gain an Ability Score Improvement level). You gain 2 sorcery points to spend only on Metamagic (added to any you already have from another source), regained on a long rest.",
    'Piercer': "You have achieved a penetrating precision in combat. Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack that deals piercing damage, you can reroll one of the attack's damage dice and must use the new roll. When you score a critical hit that deals piercing damage, you can roll one additional damage die when determining the extra piercing damage the target takes.",
    'Poisoner': "You can prepare and deliver deadly poisons. When you make a damage roll that deals poison damage, it ignores resistance to poison damage. You can apply poison to a weapon or piece of ammunition as a bonus action instead of an action. You gain proficiency with the poisoner's kit if you don't already have it. With one hour of work using a poisoner's kit and expending 50 gp worth of materials, you can create a number of doses of potent poison equal to your proficiency bonus. Once applied, the poison retains its potency for 1 minute or until you hit with the coated weapon or ammunition; a creature damaged by it must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or take 2d8 poison damage and become poisoned until the end of your next turn.",
    'Shadow Touched': "Your exposure to the Shadowfell's magic has changed you. Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. You learn the invisibility spell and one 1st-level spell of your choice from the illusion or necromancy school. You can cast each of these spells without expending a spell slot; once you cast either this way, you can't do so again with that spell until you finish a long rest (you can still cast them with spell slots you have). Spellcasting ability is the one increased by this feat.",
    'Skill Expert': "You have honed your proficiency with particular skills. Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency in one skill of your choice. Choose one skill in which you have proficiency (that isn't already benefiting from a feature like Expertise) — you gain expertise in it, doubling your proficiency bonus for checks with it.",
    'Slasher': "You've learned where to cut to have the greatest results. Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack that deals slashing damage, you can reduce its speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn. When you score a critical hit that deals slashing damage, the target has disadvantage on all attack rolls until the start of your next turn.",
    'Telekinetic': "You learn to move things with your mind. Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. You learn the mage hand cantrip, castable without verbal or somatic components, and can make the spectral hand invisible (if you already know it, its range increases by 30 feet). As a bonus action, you can try to telekinetically shove one creature within 30 feet: it makes a Strength save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + the increased ability's modifier) or is moved 5 feet toward or away from you (a creature can willingly fail this save). Spellcasting ability is the one increased by this feat.",
    'Telepathic': "You awaken the ability to mentally connect with others. Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. You can speak telepathically to any creature you can see within 60 feet of you, in a language you know; the creature understands you only if it knows that language, and can't reply telepathically. You can cast detect thoughts once without a spell slot or components, regaining the ability to do so on a long rest (also castable with a 2nd-level+ slot). Spellcasting ability is the one increased by this feat.",

    'Bountiful Luck': "Prerequisite: Halfling. Your people have extraordinary luck, which you have learned to mystically lend to your companions. When an ally you can see within 30 feet of you rolls a 1 on the d20 for an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, you can use your reaction to let the ally reroll the die (they must use the new roll). Using this ability disables your own Lucky racial trait until the end of your next turn.",
    'Dragon Fear': "Prerequisite: Dragonborn. When angered, you radiate menace. Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Instead of exhaling destructive energy, you can expend a use of your Breath Weapon to roar, forcing each creature of your choice within 30 feet to make a Wisdom save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + Charisma modifier; automatic success if it can't see or hear you). On a failed save a target is frightened of you for 1 minute, repeating the save if it takes damage.",
    'Dragon Hide': "Prerequisite: Dragonborn. You manifest scales and claws reminiscent of your draconic ancestors. Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Your scales harden: while not wearing armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier (a shield can still be used). You grow retractable claws (no action to extend/retract) that are natural weapons — an unarmed strike with them deals 1d4 + Strength modifier slashing damage instead of the normal bludgeoning.",
    'Drow High Magic': "Prerequisite: Elf (drow). You learn more of the magic typical of dark elves. You learn detect magic and can cast it at will without a spell slot. You also learn levitate and dispel magic, each castable once without a spell slot, regained on a long rest. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for all three spells.",
    'Dwarven Fortitude': "Prerequisite: Dwarf. You have the blood of dwarf heroes flowing through your veins. Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20. Whenever you take the Dodge action in combat, you can spend one Hit Die to heal yourself: roll the die, add your Constitution modifier, and regain that many hit points (minimum of 1).",
    'Elven Accuracy': "Prerequisite: Elf or half-elf. The accuracy of elves is legendary. Increase your Dexterity, Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Whenever you have advantage on an attack roll using Dexterity, Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma, you can reroll one of the dice once.",
    'Fade Away': "Prerequisite: Gnome. Your people are clever, with a knack for illusion magic. Increase your Dexterity or Intelligence by 1, to a maximum of 20. Immediately after you take damage, you can use a reaction to magically become invisible until the end of your next turn or until you attack, deal damage, or force a creature to make a saving throw. Once you use this ability, you can't do so again until you finish a short or long rest.",
    'Fey Teleportation': "Prerequisite: Elf (high). Your study of high elven lore has unlocked fey power. Increase your Intelligence or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. You learn to speak, read, and write Sylvan. You learn the misty step spell and can cast it once without expending a spell slot, regaining the ability to do so when you finish a short or long rest. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for this spell.",
    'Flames of Phlegethos': "Prerequisite: Tiefling. You learn to call on hellfire to serve your commands. Increase your Intelligence or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. When you roll fire damage for a spell you cast, you can reroll any 1s on the fire damage dice (you must use the new roll, even another 1). Whenever you cast a spell that deals fire damage, you can cause flames to wreathe you (no harm to you or your possessions) until the end of your next turn, shedding bright light 30 feet and dim light 30 feet further; any creature within 5 feet that hits you with a melee attack takes 1d4 fire damage.",
    'Infernal Constitution': "Prerequisite: Tiefling. Fiendish blood runs strong in you. Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20. You have resistance to cold and poison damage. You have advantage on saving throws against being poisoned.",
    'Orcish Fury': "Prerequisite: Half-Orc. Your fury burns tirelessly. Increase your Strength or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20. When you hit with an attack using a simple or martial weapon, you can roll one of the weapon's damage dice an additional time and add it as extra damage of the same type (once per short or long rest). Immediately after you use your Relentless Endurance trait, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack.",
    'Prodigy': "Prerequisite: Half-Elf, half-orc, or human. You have a knack for learning new things. You gain one skill proficiency, one tool proficiency, and fluency in one language, all of your choice. Choose one skill in which you have proficiency (that isn't already benefiting from something like Expertise) — you gain expertise in it, doubling your proficiency bonus for checks with it.",
    'Second Chance': "Prerequisite: Halfling. Fortune favors you when someone tries to strike you. Increase your Dexterity, Constitution, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. When a creature you can see hits you with an attack roll, you can use your reaction to force that creature to reroll. Once you use this ability, you can't use it again until you roll initiative at the start of a combat, or until you finish a short or long rest.",
    'Squat Nimbleness': "Prerequisite: Dwarf or a Small race. You are uncommonly nimble for your race. Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. Increase your walking speed by 5 feet. You gain proficiency in the Acrobatics or Athletics skill (your choice). You have advantage on any Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check you make to escape from being grappled.",
    'Svirfneblin Magic': "Prerequisite: Gnome (deep). You have inherited the innate spellcasting ability of your ancestors. You can cast nondetection on yourself at will, without needing a material component. You can also cast each of the following spells once with this ability: blindness/deafness, blur, and disguise self — regaining the ability to cast these spells when you finish a long rest. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for these spells, and you cast them at their lowest possible levels.",
    'Wood Elf Magic': "Prerequisite: Elf (wood). You learn the magic of the primeval woods revered and protected by your people. You learn one druid cantrip of your choice. You also learn the longstrider and pass without trace spells, each castable once without expending a spell slot, regaining the ability to do so when you finish a long rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for all three spells.",

    'Artificer Initiate': "You've learned some of an artificer's inventiveness. You learn one cantrip of your choice from the artificer spell list, and one 1st-level spell of your choice from that list — castable once without a spell slot, regaining the ability to do so on a long rest (you can also cast it normally with a spell slot). Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for these spells. You gain proficiency with one type of artisan's tools of your choice, and can use that type of tool as a spellcasting focus for any spell you cast that uses Intelligence as its spellcasting ability.",
    'Chef': "Time spent mastering the culinary arts has paid off. Increase your Constitution or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 20. You gain proficiency with cook's utensils if you don't already have it. As part of a short rest, given ingredients and cook's utensils, you can cook special food for a number of creatures equal to 4 + your proficiency bonus; at the end of the rest, any creature who eats it and spends Hit Dice to heal regains an extra 1d8 HP. With one hour of work, or when you finish a long rest, you can cook a number of treats equal to your proficiency bonus (each lasting 8 hours); a creature can use a bonus action to eat one and gain temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus.",
    'Eldritch Adept': "Prerequisite: Spellcasting or Pact Magic feature. Studying occult lore, you learn one Eldritch Invocation option of your choice from the warlock class. Your spellcasting ability for the invocation is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat). If the invocation has a prerequisite, you can choose it only if you're a warlock who meets that prerequisite. Whenever you gain a level, you can replace the invocation with another one from the warlock class.",
    'Revenant Blade': "Prerequisite: Elf. You are descended from a master of the double-bladed scimitar, and some of that mastery has passed on to you. Increase your Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20. While holding a double-bladed scimitar with two hands, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class. A double-bladed scimitar has the finesse property when you wield it.",

    'Aberrant Dragonmark': "Prerequisite: no other dragonmark. You have manifested an aberrant dragonmark; determine its appearance and the flaw associated with it. Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20. You learn a cantrip of your choice from the sorcerer spell list, and choose a 1st-level spell from that list which you learn and can cast through your mark once per short or long rest (Constitution is your spellcasting ability for these). You can also cast the spells using spell slots you have. When you cast the 1st-level spell through your mark, you can expend one of your Hit Dice and roll it: on an even number, you gain that many temporary hit points; on an odd number, one random creature within 30 feet (not including you) takes force damage equal to the number rolled — or you take the damage if no other creature is in range. You also develop a random flaw from the Aberrant Dragonmark Flaws table (roll a d8): (1) your mark is a source of constant physical pain; (2) your mark whispers to you, unclearly; (3) when stressed, the mark hisses audibly; (4) the skin around the mark is burned, scaly, or withered; (5) animals are uneasy around you; (6) you have a mood swing whenever you use your mark; (7) your looks change slightly whenever you use the mark; (8) you have horrific nightmares after using your mark.",

    'Scion of the Outer Planes': "Prerequisite: Planescape Campaign. Your connection to an Outer Plane infuses you with the energy there. Choose a type of plane from the Planar Infusion table — your choice gives you resistance to a damage type and the ability to cast a cantrip, without material components: Chaotic Outer Plane grants poison resistance and minor illusion; Evil Outer Plane grants necrotic resistance and chill touch; Good Outer Plane grants radiant resistance and sacred flame; Lawful Outer Plane grants force resistance and guidance; the Outlands grants psychic resistance and mage hand. Your spellcasting ability for the cantrip is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat).",
    'Agent of Order': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Scion of the Outer Planes (lawful outer plane). You can channel cosmic forces of order. Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 20. Once per turn, when you damage a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself, you can deal an extra 1d8 force damage and force a Wisdom save (DC = 8 + proficiency bonus + your Scion of the Outer Planes spellcasting modifier) as spectral bindings (chains or similar) try to ensnare it; on a failed save the target is restrained until the start of your next turn. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Baleful Scion': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Scion of the Outer Planes (evil outer plane). You can channel cosmic forces of evil. Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 20. Once per turn, when you damage a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself, you can also deal 1d6 + your proficiency bonus necrotic damage to it and regain that many hit points. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Cartomancer': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Spellcasting Feature. You have learned to channel your magic through a deck of cards, usable as your spellcasting focus. You learn the prestidigitation cantrip, usable to create stage-magic illusions, concealing its verbal and somatic components as ordinary conversation and card handling. When you finish a long rest, you can imbue one spell you have a slot for from your class list (casting time of 1 action) into a card; it remains imbued for 8 hours, and you can bonus-action flourish the card to cast the spell within (the card then loses its magic).",
    'Cohort of Chaos': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Scion of the Outer Planes (chaotic outer plane). You can channel cosmic forces of chaos. Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 20. When you roll a 1 or a 20 on an attack roll or a saving throw, roll a d4 to trigger a random Chaotic Flare, lasting until the end of your next turn (a new flare can't occur until the current one ends): (1) Battle Fury — a creature of your choice you can see gets advantage on attack rolls and disadvantage on ability checks; (2) Disruption Field — creatures starting their turn within 5 feet of you, or moving into that area, take 1d8 force damage; (3) Unbound — you can use some or all of your walking speed to teleport once when you move; (4) Wailing Winds — winds swirl in a 15-foot sphere centered on you, giving you and others in it disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws.",
    'Outlands Envoy': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Scion of the Outer Planes (the Outlands). You have spent significant time in Sigil or the Outlands. Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 20. You learn the misty step and tongues spells; you can cast each once using this feat without a spell slot (tongues requires no material components this way), regaining that ability when you finish a long rest. You can also cast these spells with spell slots you have. Spellcasting ability is the one chosen for Scion of the Outer Planes.",
    'Planar Wanderer': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Scion of the Outer Planes. You can draw on the forces of the multiverse to survive cosmic extremes and traverse its realms. When you finish a long rest, you gain resistance to acid, cold, or fire damage (your choice) until your next long rest. As an action, you can concentrate on a portal within 5 feet you're aware of and make a DC 20 Intelligence (Arcana) check: on a failure you take 3d8 psychic damage and can't try again on that portal until a long rest; on a success you force it open or closed for 1 hour, during which it ignores its portal key unless a creature using the key succeeds on its own DC 20 Intelligence (Arcana) check as an action. You know the direction to the last planar portal you used while you and it share a plane; as an action (usable once until a long rest) you can detect any portals within 30 feet not behind total cover.",
    'Righteous Heritor': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Scion of the Outer Planes (good outer plane). You can channel cosmic forces of good. Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 20. When you or a creature within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to reduce that damage by 1d10 + your proficiency bonus. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",

    'Strixhaven Initiate': "You have studied some magical theory and learned a few spells associated with Strixhaven University. Choose one of Strixhaven's colleges: Lorehold, Prismari, Quandrix, Silverquill, or Witherbloom. You learn two cantrips and one 1st-level spell based on the college chosen (Lorehold: light/sacred flame/thaumaturgy plus a 1st-level cleric or wizard spell; Prismari: fire bolt/prestidigitation/ray of frost plus a 1st-level bard or sorcerer spell; Quandrix: druidcraft/guidance/mage hand plus a 1st-level druid or wizard spell; Silverquill: sacred flame/thaumaturgy/vicious mockery plus a 1st-level bard or cleric spell; Witherbloom: chill touch/druidcraft/spare the dying plus a 1st-level druid or wizard spell). You can cast the chosen 1st-level spell once without a spell slot, regaining the ability on a long rest (also castable with slots you have). Spellcasting ability is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat).",
    'Strixhaven Mascot': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Strixhaven Initiate. You have learned to summon a Strixhaven mascot to assist you. You can cast find familiar as a ritual; your familiar can take the form of your college's mascot (a spirit statue for Lorehold, an art elemental for Prismari, a fractal for Quandrix, an inkling for Silverquill, or a pest for Witherbloom). When you take the Attack action, you can forgo one attack to let your mascot familiar make an attack of its own with its reaction. If your familiar is within 60 feet, you can use your action to teleport, swapping places with it (fails and is wasted if your destination space is too small). Once you teleport this way, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a 2nd-level+ spell slot to do it again.",

    'Divinely Favored': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Dragonlance Campaign. A god chose you to carry a spark of their power. You learn one cleric cantrip, augury, and one 1st-level spell chosen by your alignment (Evil: a warlock spell; Good: a cleric spell; Neutral: a druid spell). You can cast the chosen 1st-level spell and augury each once without a spell slot, regaining the ability when you finish a long rest (also castable with slots you have). Spellcasting ability is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat); a holy symbol can serve as your spellcasting focus for spells using that ability.",
    'Initiate of High Sorcery': "Prerequisites: Dragonlance Campaign; Sorcerer, Wizard, or Mage of High Sorcery. You've received training from magic-users affiliated with the Mages of High Sorcery. Choose one of the three moons of Krynn to influence your magic: Nuitari (black), Lunitari (red), or Solinari (white). You learn one wizard cantrip and two 1st-level spells per the Lunar Spells table (Nuitari: choose two from dissonant whispers/false life/hex/ray of sickness; Lunitari: choose two from color spray/disguise self/feather fall/longstrider; Solinari: choose two from comprehend languages/detect evil and good/protection from evil and good/shield). You can cast each chosen 1st-level spell once without a spell slot, regaining the ability when you finish a long rest (also castable with slots you have). Spellcasting ability is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat).",
    'Adept of the Black Robes': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Initiate of High Sorcery (Nuitari). You chose the moon Nuitari, and your ambition and loyalty to the Order of the Black Robes have been recognized. Ambitious Magic: you learn one 2nd-level enchantment or necromancy spell, castable once without a spell slot (regaining the ability on a long rest, or castable with slots you have of the appropriate level); spellcasting ability matches your Initiate of High Sorcery choice. Life Channel: when a creature you can see within 60 feet fails a saving throw against a damaging spell you cast, you can expend Hit Dice equal to the spell's level, roll and total them, and add that total as extra damage the creature takes.",
    'Adept of the Red Robes': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Initiate of High Sorcery (Lunitari). You chose the moon Lunitari, and your dedication to balance has been recognized by the Order of the Red Robes. Insightful Magic: you learn one 2nd-level illusion or transmutation spell, castable once without a spell slot (regaining the ability on a long rest, or castable with slots you have of the appropriate level); spellcasting ability matches your Initiate of High Sorcery choice. Magical Balance: when you roll 9 or lower on the d20 for an attack roll or ability check, you can treat the roll as a 10. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Adept of the White Robes': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Initiate of High Sorcery (Solinari). You chose the moon Solinari, and your oath to better the world through magic has been recognized by the Order of the White Robes. Protective Magic: you learn one 2nd-level abjuration or divination spell, castable once without a spell slot (regaining the ability on a long rest, or castable with slots you have of the appropriate level); spellcasting ability matches your Initiate of High Sorcery choice. Protective Ward: reaction when you or a creature within 30 feet takes damage — expend a spell slot, roll a number of d6s equal to its level, and reduce the damage taken by the total plus your spellcasting ability modifier.",
    'Squire of Solamnia': "Prerequisites: Dragonlance Campaign; Fighter, Paladin, or Knight of Solamnia. Your training in the ways of the Knights of Solamnia grants you these benefits. Mount Up: mounting or dismounting costs only 5 feet of movement. Precise Strike: once per turn, when you make a weapon attack roll, you can give it advantage; if it hits, roll a d8 and add the result to the damage (a use is expended only if the attack hits). Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest. Note: Knights of Solamnia belong to only one order at a time; most begin in the Order of the Crown before moving to another, retaining any earlier Knight of Solamnia feats even after switching orders.",
    'Knight of the Crown': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Squire of Solamnia. You are a Knight of Solamnia aligned with the Order of the Crown, which extols cooperation, loyalty, and obedience. Increase your Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20. Commanding Rally: as a bonus action, command one ally within 30 feet who can see or hear you to attack — they can immediately make one weapon attack as a reaction, and on a hit add a rolled d8 to the damage. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Knight of the Rose': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Squire of Solamnia. You are a Knight of Solamnia aligned with the Order of the Rose, known for leadership, justice, and wisdom. Increase your Constitution, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Bolstering Rally: as a bonus action, encourage one creature you can see within 30 feet (yourself included) who can see or hear you — they gain temporary hit points equal to 1d8 + your proficiency bonus + the increased ability's modifier. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Knight of the Sword': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Squire of Solamnia. You are a Knight of Solamnia aligned with the Order of the Sword, devoted to heroism and courage. Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Demoralizing Strike: once per turn, when you hit with a weapon attack, force a Wisdom save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + the increased ability's modifier) — on a failure the target is frightened of you until the end of your next turn; on a success it has disadvantage on its next attack roll before the end of its next turn. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",

    'Gift of the Chromatic Dragon': "You've manifested some of the power of chromatic dragons. Chromatic Infusion: as a bonus action, touch a simple or martial weapon and infuse it with acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison — for the next minute it deals an extra 1d4 damage of that type on a hit; usable once per long rest. Reactive Resistance: when you take acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage, you can use your reaction to gain resistance to that instance of damage. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Gift of the Gem Dragon': "You've manifested some of the power of gem dragons. Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Telekinetic Reprisal: when you take damage from a creature within 10 feet of you, you can use your reaction to emanate telekinetic energy — the creature makes a Strength save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + the increased ability's modifier); on a failure it takes 2d8 force damage and is pushed up to 10 feet away, or half damage with no push on a success. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Gift of the Metallic Dragon': "You've manifested some of the power of metallic dragons. Draconic Healing: you learn the cure wounds spell, castable once without a spell slot (regaining the ability on a long rest, or castable with slots you have); spellcasting ability is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you gain the feat). Protective Wings: when you or another creature within 5 feet you can see is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to manifest spectral wings, granting the target a bonus to its AC against that attack equal to your proficiency bonus (potentially causing it to miss). Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",

    'Strike of the Giants': "Prerequisites: proficiency with martial weapons, or Giant Foundling. You have absorbed primeval magic giving you an echo of the might of giants. Choose one benefit; once per turn, when you hit with a melee weapon attack or a thrown ranged weapon attack, you can imbue it: Cloud Strike (extra 1d4 thunder; a creature that fails a Wisdom save also can't see you until you attack, cast a spell, or the start of your next turn); Fire Strike (extra 1d10 fire); Frost Strike (extra 1d6 cold; a creature that fails a Constitution save has its speed reduced to 0 until the start of your next turn); Hill Strike (extra 1d6 of the weapon's damage type; a creature that fails a Strength save falls prone); Stone Strike (extra 1d6 force; a creature that fails a Strength save is pushed 10 feet in a straight line away from you); Storm Strike (extra 1d6 lightning; a creature that fails a Constitution save has disadvantage on attack rolls until the start of your next turn). Save DC = 8 + proficiency bonus + your Strength or Constitution modifier. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Ember of the Fire Giant': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Strike of the Giants (fire). You've manifested the fiery combat emblematic of fire giants. Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 20. Born of Flame: you have resistance to fire damage. Searing Ignition: when you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with a burst of flame in a 15-foot-radius sphere centered on you — each creature of your choice makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + the increased ability's modifier); on a failure a creature takes 1d8 + proficiency bonus fire damage and is blinded until the start of your next turn, or takes half damage only on a success. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus (max once per turn), regained on a long rest.",
    'Fury of the Frost Giant': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Strike of the Giants (frost). You've manifested the icy might emblematic of frost giants. Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 20. Born of Ice: you have resistance to cold damage. Frigid Retaliation: immediately after a creature within 30 feet you can see hits and damages you, you can use your reaction to retaliate with conjured ice — the creature makes a Constitution save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + the increased ability's modifier); on a failure it takes 1d8 + proficiency bonus cold damage and its speed is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Guile of the Cloud Giant': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Strike of the Giants (cloud). You've manifested the confounding magic emblematic of cloud giants. Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Cloudy Escape: when a creature you can see hits you with an attack roll, you can use your reaction to gain resistance to that attack's damage, then teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Keenness of the Stone Giant': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Strike of the Giants (stone). You've manifested the physical talents emblematic of stone giants. Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 20. Cavernous Sight: you gain darkvision out to 60 feet (or +60 feet range if you already have darkvision). Stone Throw: as a bonus action, make a magical ranged spell attack with a rock, range 60 feet, using the increased ability as your spellcasting ability — on a hit it deals 1d10 force damage and the target makes a Strength save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + that modifier) or falls prone. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Soul of the Storm Giant': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Strike of the Giants (storm). You've manifested the tempest magic emblematic of storm giants. Increase your Strength, Wisdom, or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20. Maelstrom Aura: as a bonus action, surround yourself with a 10-foot aura of wind and lightning (blocked by total cover) lasting until the start of your next turn or until you're incapacitated. While active, you resist lightning and thunder damage; attack rolls against you have disadvantage; and whenever another creature starts its turn in the aura, it makes a Strength save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + the increased ability's modifier) or has its speed halved until the start of its next turn. Uses equal to your proficiency bonus, regained on a long rest.",
    'Vigor of the Hill Giant': "Prerequisites: 4th level, Strike of the Giants (hill). You've manifested the resilience emblematic of hill giants. Increase your Strength, Constitution, or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 20. Bulwark: reaction when subjected to an effect that would move you 5+ feet or knock you prone — you aren't moved and don't fall prone. Iron Stomach: eating during a short rest and spending Hit Dice to heal restores additional HP equal to your Constitution modifier + proficiency bonus.",
    'Rune Shaper': "Prerequisites: Spellcasting Feature or Rune Carver. You've studied the magic of Giant runes. Comprehend Languages: learn the spell, castable once without a spell slot, regained on a long rest (also castable with slots you have). Rune Magic: know a number of runes equal to half your proficiency bonus (rounded down), each corresponding to a 1st-level spell — Cloud (fog cloud), Death (inflict wounds), Dragon (chromatic orb), Enemy (disguise self), Fire (burning hands), Friend (speak with animals), Frost (armor of Agathys), Hill (goodberry), Journey (longstrider), King (command), Mountain (entangle), Stone (sanctuary), Storm (thunderwave). On a long rest, inscribe each known rune onto a touched nonmagical object; you temporarily learn each inscribed rune's spell until your next long rest, castable with a spell slot while carrying the object. You can also invoke an inscribed rune to cast its spell once without a spell slot or components, regaining that ability on a long rest. Spellcasting ability is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you take this feat). Replace one known rune with another on each level gained.",
})

